<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Life of Columba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 700</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Vita Columbae</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Life of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/columba">Columba</a> is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> life of Saint Columba, founder of the monastery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iona">Iona</a>, written by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adomnan">Adomnán</a>, the ninth abbot of Iona, around 700. Arranged in three books of prophecies, miracles and visions, it is the most important source for early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a>, Iona and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picts">Picts</a>, and for the kingship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aedan-mac-gabrain">Áedán mac Gabráin</a>.</p></div>
